Separate forward and reverse logistics create inefficiencies and costs preventing economic remanufacturing viability. Integrated core exchange logistics capture used products when new ones are delivered, creating bidirectional logistics minimizing empty vehicle return trips. Exchange logistics create automatic core returns reducing collection barriers.

Core deposits create financial incentives for responsible return behaviour. Integrated logistics enable operational efficiency where remanufacturing becomes self-sustaining without requiring separate recovery infrastructure. Exchange-based systems create market conditions where product cores become valuable assets rather than waste.